  "chunk": "6\nFigure 1: Left: Average number of points with standard error bars. Right:\nAverage number of moves per game with standard errors bars. (I) denotes the\nbasic prompt and (II) denotes the advanced prompt.\nthat the models provided by Anthropic are more capable of playing the game.\nThe difference between the variants of Claude appear minimal. Interestingly,\nthere seems to be no difference between using the basic prompt (indicated by\nI) and the advanced prompt (indicated by II), while you may suspect that de-\ntailed instructions on the internal mechanics of the game, including multiple\nkey gameplay insights, should improve performance. For human players, we\nsuspect that access to a detailed manual has a significant impact on the ability\nto play the gameZork. Lastly, the results suggest that there is no difference\nwhen ‘thinking’ is enabled across all three providers. Although Figure 1 does\nnot show the difference between ‘non-thinking’ and ‘thinking’ for Gemini and",
